Mechanism: The BGP session between leaf_router_0_0 (AS 65200) and spine_router_0_1 (AS 65101) uses the /31 link 172.16.0.9/31 (leaf) — 172.16.0.8/31 (spine). With leaf_router_0_0:eth1 down, the TCP session to port 179 cannot be maintained, so FRR on the leaf keeps the neighbor in Active and resets the connection. Traffic still flows host-to-host because the alternate uplink via spine_router_0_0 remains up and carries the routes.

